{"description":"Wire a human-in-the-loop approval channel so a default-deny permission request is SURFACED to a human, not silently denied: when code policy cannot decide, steward raises a structured approval prompt (ACP elicitation or an equivalent channel), records the human decision as a typed artifact, and resumes deterministically on the response.","acceptanceCriteria":"A permission request the policy cannot decide is escalated to a human and blocks until answered or times out to deny.\nThe human decision is recorded as a typed artifact and drives the gate deterministically.\nTests cover approve, deny and timeout paths.\nNo approval path requires a live TTY on the steward host."}